## How to Run the Project

### 1. Clone the repository

git clone <your-repository-url>

### 2. Navigate into the project directory

cd Sales-Forecasting

### 3. Install the required Python libraries

pip install pandas numpy matplotlib scikit-learn jupyter

### 4. Open the notebook

jupyter notebook

Open:

Sales Project.ipynb

Make sure the dataset is located at:

data/Sample - Superstore.csv

Then run the notebook from beginning to end.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates how historical sales data can be transformed into a monthly forecasting dataset and used to build and evaluate simple machine learning models.

The analysis shows an overall upward sales trend and noticeable monthly seasonality. The seasonal Linear Regression model achieved a lower MAE than the baseline model on the 2017 test data, showing that incorporating monthly patterns improved the forecasts in this evaluation.

The project also demonstrates an important limitation of simple forecasting models: while they can capture general patterns, they may not accurately predict unusually large sales spikes.

